1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,500
LabWeaver links materials, approvals, environments, access, resources, and evidence into one traceable lab journey.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:19,500
Six domain services coordinate through PostgreSQL authoritative state and NATS JetStream events.

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:29,500
Container and KubeVirt VM share one environment contract while dedicated executors isolate runtime failures.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:44,500
The teacher uploads public-safe material and first checks LLM egress and protected-content boundaries.

5
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:59,500
AgentRuns create Environment and Evaluation candidates; deterministic tools validate them and candidates never execute automatically.

6
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:14,500
Independent teacher approval publishes immutable releases with source, validation result, and Runtime identity.

7
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:26,500
The administrator handles a request produced by the formal Work/Agent path without fabricating a missing request UI.

8
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:39,500
ResourceQuota and time-bounded Lease readback give capacity allocation an explicit scope, lifetime, and audit trail.

9
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:52,500
The student creates a Container from a teacher-published template while Environment Service owns lifecycle state.

10
00:01:53,000 --> 00:02:05,500
An AccessGrant is issued after ready; network reachability and business authorization remain separate.

11
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:18,500
The student edits, compiles, and runs the public C++ sample in the browser terminal.

12
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:29,500
Resize, disconnect, and reconnect return to the same environment while the control plane tracks lifecycle state.

13
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:43,500
The KubeVirt Provider brings Linux system labs under the same Environment contract as Container labs.

14
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:57,500
ConsoleCapability converts short-lived authorization into noVNC access without exposing VMI endpoints directly.

15
00:02:58,000 --> 00:03:11,500
A dedicated executor reconciles stop/start or recovery and preserves environment identity across the transition.

16
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:24,500
This rehearsal keeps its Fixture boundary explicit; real VMI/noVNC success still belongs to #126 connected acceptance.

17
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:36,500
Freezing creates an immutable FrozenSubmission reference instead of relying on a mutable workspace or screenshot.

18
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:49,500
Object Version, SHA-256, source commit, and runtime identity form one auditable evidence chain.

19
00:03:50,000 --> 00:04:01,500
After the AccessGrant revision changes, the active session closes and the old capability becomes invalid.

20
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:14,500
A reconnect receives a stable diagnostic; identity, policy, or version mismatch fails closed.

21
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:29,500
Environment deletion and residue-free readback close the loop from authoring through evidence and resource reclamation.
